{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"prompt\": \"Use case: stylized-concept. Create a Minecraft builder reference sheet, landscape approximately 3:2, plain light background, crisp voxel style, vanilla Minecraft blocks only, no characters or animals. Two views side by side: LEFT straight-on front elevation, orthographic; RIGHT three-quarter front-right view at the same block scale. Show the same complete building in both views with clear separation and margins. Skilled human builder quality: real massing and depth, projecting counters and upper storey, recessed framed openings, real roof verges, eaves and ridge, stairs/slabs/fences/walls/trapdoors/lantern details. No invented curved architectural components.\\nSite: traditional German town bakery seen from a gravel lane, tall gable end facing street. Ground storey charcoal deepslate brick on smooth darker plinth. Centred spruce front door with glass transom between two wide three-pane shop windows. Each has projecting spruce-slab sales counter and folded-back spruce shutters. Tan stripped-spruce lintel beam across entire front; exactly five spruce brackets support upper storey projecting one block over pavement. Upper storey classic Fachwerk: stripped-spruce posts, sill/head beams and breast rail; bright white panels; darker spruce stair diagonal braces in end panels. Two 2x2 windows with red-tulip flower boxes. Steep grey slate roof, dark tiles with lighter mottling, spruce barge boards, high ridge running back from street. Timbered front gable with collar beam, king post, two small attic windows and open central loft door with shutters. Above loft door stripped-spruce hoist beam projects beyond verge, iron chain suspends barrel. Wrought-style hanging sign made from vanilla sign and chain, reading exactly \\\"Bäckerei\\\", on spruce arm at right corner; lanterns under overhang.\\nSet back on right: lower single-storey cobbled-deepslate bakehouse wing with its own small slate gable. At back red-brick bread oven projects into yard with stepped brick stair/slab barrel-vault approximation. Slim brick chimney with dark band and campfire smoke rises to height 17, about two-thirds main roof height. Behind house spruce-fenced yard with stacked spruce firewood, barrels, hay bales, small wheat patch and exactly two small spruce trees. Arrange right view to expose rear-yard features as far as physical occlusion allows.\\nDimensions in Minecraft blocks: site 24 wide x 32 deep; main house 11 wide x 15 deep; bakehouse wing 5 wide plus oven; two storeys and steep attic; main ridge 21 high; chimney 17 high.\\nUse these exact block ids as material specification (do not print a giant palette on the sheet):\\nground_walls: deepslate_bricks, deepslate_brick_stairs, deepslate_brick_slab, deepslate_brick_wall.\\nplinth: polished_deepslate, polished_deepslate_stairs, polished_deepslate_slab.\\nwing_walls: cobbled_deepslate, cobbled_deepslate_stairs, cobbled_deepslate_slab, cobbled_deepslate_wall.\\nframe: stripped_spruce_log, stripped_spruce_wood, spruce_stairs.\\ndaub: white_wool.\\nroof: cobbled_deepslate, deepslate_tiles, polished_deepslate, deepslate_tile_stairs, deepslate_tile_slab.\\nroof_eave: polished_blackstone_bricks, polished_blackstone_brick_stairs, polished_blackstone_brick_slab.\\nroof_ridge: deepslate_brick_slab.\\nverge_floor: spruce_planks, spruce_slab, spruce_stairs.\\noven: bricks, brick_stairs, brick_slab, brick_wall.\\nchimney_band: deepslate_bricks.\\nglass: glass_pane.\\nstreet: gravel, cobbled_deepslate, cobblestone, mossy_cobblestone.\\nyard: grass_block, podzol, coarse_dirt, dirt_path, farmland, wheat, spruce_log, spruce_leaves.\\nAvailable functional/decor ids: spruce_door, spruce_trapdoor, spruce_fence, spruce_fence_gate, spruce_hanging_sign, spruce_wall_sign, lantern, campfire, candle, white_candle, iron_chain, potted_red_tulip, potted_poppy, flower_pot, smoker, blast_furnace, furnace, barrel, hay_block, composter, grindsto